    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Neon Heat Disease - Live In Los Angeles (2025) is the first live album by Beat, a supergroup featuring former King Crimson members Adrian Belew and Tony Levin, alongside virtuoso guitarist Steve Vai and Tool drummer Danny Carey. The album captures a sold-out 2024 performance in Los Angeles, presenting live reinterpretations of King Crimson’s seminal 1980s work from the albums Discipline, Beat, and Three of a Perfect Pair. The music is characterized by energetic, precise playing that balances the original material’s complexity with the distinctive styles of the new lineup, resulting in a nimble, gritty rock sound that contrasts with King Crimson’s more orchestral recent live efforts.\n\nThis live recording, released through Inside Out Music and Sony Music, is available in multiple formats including a deluxe triple LP, 2CD+Blu-ray set, and digital HD audio. The concert was mixed by renowned engineer Bob Clearmountain, ensuring a polished yet dynamic sound. Critics have praised the album for its faithful yet fresh approach, highlighting the band’s technical prowess and the vitality of veteran musicians averaging around 70 years old. The Blu-ray edition, featuring 5.1 surround sound and 24-bit stereo, also showcases a visually minimalistic stage show focused on musicianship, reinforcing the album’s appeal to progressive rock and King Crimson fans alike.",
